  "notes": "{裂|さ}く means to tear or split something apart by force.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {裂|さ}ける (intransitive, to be torn/split)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {紙|かみ}を{裂|さ}く: to tear paper\n- {布|ぬの}を{裂|さ}く: to rip cloth\n- {二人|ふたり}を{裂|さ}く: to separate two people (figurative)\n\nDON'T CONFUSE:\n- {裂|さ}く: to tear, rip\n- {咲|さ}く: to bloom (flowers) — same pronunciation, different meaning\n- {割|さ}く: to spare (time/resources) — different kanji, same pronunciation",
